For right-to-left text, Ladybird finds where a range is drawn, and which
offset a point hits, from the shaped glyphs’ clusters and positions.
Blink works from its shape results the same way: Its FragmentItem::
LocalRect() and ShapeResult::CaretOffsetForHitTest() both build on
ShapeResult::CaretPositionForOffset(). WebKit has FontCascade::
adjustSelectionRectForText() and FontCascade::offsetForPosition() for
that. And Gecko has nsTextFrame::GetCharacterOffsetAtFramePoint(), and
it paints each selected segment of a frame in its nsTextFrame::
PaintTextWithSelection().
